HFHDR|item=helium-film|file=sims/helium-film/PREDICTION-HELIUM-FILM.hbp|date=2026-11-09|request_date=2026-11-08|seat=cloud|base_commit=ac5b1580c4ad50ed2bc54e0762d1bb57f6ddee83 (written against ac5b158; committed on main ea68fc2 or later, whose later commits do not touch sims/)|lanes_read_at=c8664c195aea5de097b4eaff53b0e5aecdd60086 (6 commits behind base_commit; none of the 6 touch sims/)|toolchain=1.81.0|engine_code_written=0|engine_runs=0|frozen_before_measurement=1|lanes=lane1-statics-transfer, lane2-gp-mechanism, lane3-controls-limits|judges=judge-lowT, referee|owner_question=can the integer engines simulate the superfluid helium film: about 30 nm thick, climbs the wall, flows over the rim, drips|writes_external=0|fix_pass=the final critic returned FIX_FIRST with 7 blocking items and 13 fix items; the 7 blocking items and 12 fixes were applied before the freeze, and the 13th fix item, a list of checks the critic found correct, was rechecked; a verification of that pass found 2 more blocking items and 17 minor ones, and a second pass fixed them before the freeze; a verification of the second pass found 2 more blocking items and 10 minor ones, and a third pass fixed them before the freeze; a verification of the third pass found 1 more blocking item and 8 minor ones, and a fourth pass fixed them before the freeze (the blocking item by stating in HF-G07 what its precondition does not cover); every moved number was recomputed exactly (record of the four passes: sims/helium-film/CHANGES.txt, committed beside this file in the freeze commit; the scratch calculators that it and HFDEF basis.* name stay outside the repository, and so do the engine plan and open_constants.txt that it cites, until the code commit)|json=0
HFDEF|term=format|meaning=one record per line; fields split at the first = sign; values keep their spaces (as docs/handoffs/acer-usb-ram-records-2026-10-19/FABLE5-LAW-LEDGER.hbp does) and never contain the bar character, so abs(x) stands for the absolute value; A means Angstrom; xi is the GP length unit|json=0
HFDEF|term=cite.DB98|meaning=R. J. Donnelly and C. F. Barenghi 1998, J. Phys. Chem. Ref. Data 27, 1217 (online tables pages.uoregon.edu/rjd)|json=0
HFDEF|term=method.statics|meaning=statics engine sims/helium-film/statics: Rust 1.81, std only, integers only; exact rationals over an in-crate bignum; n-th roots by integer bracketing N^n <= X 10^(n s) < (N+1)^n; hbar from h and the K08 pi bracket; every printed decimal rounded outward; one receipt line per row regenerated byte for byte in CI and by the stdlib integer referee|json=0
HFDEF|term=method.gp|meaning=GP engine sims/helium-film/gp: Rust 1.81, std plus aether's shadowcat (SHA-256 only), integers only, numerics K57, geometries K58; records every 2 time units as raw integer sums (the HF-N02 dispersion strip also evaluates its mode coefficients at every step and records each sign change, K57); observables on cell edges follow cell.edge; the reader hf-read forms observables in rationals; q (HF-G05) is a central difference of the 2-unit records, so q and v_rim = q/Gamma_top exist only on records with both neighbours, 2 <= t <= t_end - 2 (t_end the run's last record), and every read of q or v_rim, and every bound on them, uses only those records|json=0
HFDEF|term=record.CONST|meaning=an input: id, name, value (an exact decimal where numeric), units, tag, source, verified (1 or 0), an optional note, used_by|json=0
HFDEF|term=record.PREDICT|meaning=a frozen claim: id, kind, tag, control, fixed_by_inputs, statement, predicted, verdict_rule, method, falsifier, inputs, cost, from|json=0
HFDEF|term=record.LANEROW|meaning=what happened to each of the 39 lane rows: KEPT, RESTATED, MERGED, MOVED or DROPPED, with the judges reason|json=0
HFDEF|term=kind.REAL_HELIUM|meaning=a statement about liquid 4He computed from literature inputs; never a GP output|json=0
HFDEF|term=kind.MODEL_EXACT|meaning=a property of the GP model or of its discretization that has an exact value; the tolerance bands around it are estimates|json=0
HFDEF|term=kind.MECHANISM|meaning=the GP model shows the effect in its own units; it carries no helium number|json=0
HFDEF|term=kind.NUMERICS|meaning=what the integer engine itself must do|json=0
HFDEF|term=kind.HONEST_LIMIT|meaning=what this study does not and cannot give about helium, made checkable|json=0
HFDEF|term=tag.REPORTED|meaning=a literature value with its citation (CONST rows)|json=0
HFDEF|term=tag.DERIVED|meaning=follows exactly from stated, verified inputs; the row certifies arithmetic or an exact model identity|json=0
HFDEF|term=tag.CONJECTURE|meaning=anything else: a measured engine outcome with a frozen band, or a row fed by an UNVERIFIED input|json=0
HFDEF|term=tag.DEFINED|meaning=CONST rows only: a design choice of the model or the engine, an input and not a claim|json=0
HFDEF|term=rule.unverified|meaning=a row that uses a constant with verified=0 in its verdict is tagged CONJECTURE, whatever its arithmetic; a verified=0 constant printed only as context does not change the tag (K27 in HF-S14, K19 in HF-L03)|json=0
HFDEF|term=verdict|meaning=one convention for every row: MET if every frozen claim of the row holds when its method is run, NOT_MET otherwise; a row whose claim is negative (for example that a spread exceeds a bound, or that no film forms) is MET when that negative claim holds; INCONCLUSIVE only where the row names the precondition (only HF-G07 names one); a row any part of whose method was not run reads NOT_MET|json=0
HFDEF|term=control.NEGATIVE|meaning=an engine run in which the effect must be absent or an engine check must fail; these rows can come out NOT_MET on a real outcome: HF-G03 (its part a; part b is a bug check), HF-G10, HF-G11, HF-G12, HF-N01|json=0
HFDEF|term=fixed_by_inputs|meaning=1 marks a row whose verdict is fixed once its inputs are frozen (only an arithmetic slip or a re-read of a source can flip it); such rows certify arithmetic and never count as negative controls|json=0
HFDEF|term=frozen|meaning=every PREDICT row was frozen before any engine code was written or run (frozen_before_measurement = 1 for the whole file)|json=0
HFDEF|term=numbers|meaning=certified intervals are rounded outward; x +/- u means the certified interval must lie inside [x - u, x + u]; a list of values with one +/- applies it to each|json=0
HFDEF|term=gp.equation|meaning=i dpsi/dt = [-(1/2) Lap + V(r,t) - mu_ref - 2abs(psi)^2 + (3/2)abs(psi)^4] psi in GP units hbar = m = n0 = c0 = 1; V = g y + U_w(z; C3) [+ barrier]|json=0
HFDEF|term=cell.edge|meaning=cell centres sit at x = (i + 1/2) dx and y = -2 + (j + 1/2) dx, so at dx = 1/2 and at dx = 1/4 every named integer row or column is a cell edge: the rows y = 56, 64, 80, 96, 128 of G0 (h = 24, 32, 48, 64, 96), the rows y = 40, 32, 24 of G0d, the meniscus columns 3 xi from the faces (x = 61 and x = 83 in G0 and G0d), the cap-top columns (x = 72 in G0, x = 104 in G1) and the mirror axis x = 0. Each observable named at such a row or column (a thickness, a crossing height, a coverage, Gamma_top and its wall-layer part, s_top) is the mean of its values on the two straddling rows or columns, an exact rational, and it is compared with the 1D reference at the exact h. At the mirror axis the two straddling columns are mirror images, so the mean is the first column. Reason: ds/dh = -0.0951 at h = 24, so a nearest-row choice could move s by 0.024 xi at dx = 1/2 and 0.012 xi at dx = 1/4, enough to flip HF-G02 (iii). A named point on a cell corner (K61 A and B) is the cell that K61 names|json=0
HFDEF|term=basis.statics|meaning=the frozen statics numbers come from scratch calculators, not engine code: lane 1 hand.py, hand2.py, hand3.py (40-digit Decimal), the referee check1.py (50 digits) and the synthesis statics.py (60 digits; sha256 f6293186f4a69efa..., output statics.txt f4787af16cb7338c...); the fix pass added exact_extra.py (Fractions, the K08 pi bracket and integer root bracketing; sha256 fef1051e2184eea7..., output exact_extra.out 384b12089e7e94e3...) for the HF-S12 reverse window, the HF-L02 margins and the HF-S10 model (c) in closed form with d = w^4|json=0
HFDEF|term=basis.gp|meaning=the frozen 1D-reduced GP numbers come from the synthesis float design relaxation gp1d.py (sha256 4ad1d97329ea84e5...; engine discretization: 4th-order stencil, dx = 1/2, cell centres at (i + 1/2) dx; outputs film4.txt f9876feb90752e27..., gap4.txt d8c52c7c78759ef1..., wet4.txt 4fefa2557a5f086c..., wet4_c0.txt 87937613565d51f3..., ratio4.txt bdb41da9f324903f..., extra.txt 3a1763dc19b3adfc...), within 0.15 percent of the referee film1d.py (2nd order, dx = 0.05); scratch only, not engine code; the engine must reproduce them. The fix pass recomputed the numbers it moved without floats: exact_wet.py ports the gp1d.py relaxation to integer fixed point at 2^64 and evaluates every energy as an exact rational (sha256 33b8d6fdc7360452..., output exact_wet.out 21bbf7e8e78bf680...; under the draft np.diff energy it reproduces wet4.txt and wet4_c0.txt to every printed digit), exact_angle.py the Young angles and the discrete sigma_lv (64b197b4bf48c884..., output 4c3b14b273bb7326...), and exact_eig.py the HF-G08 thresholds by exact inertia counts (3e39d2d6292478e4..., output 40faf5db3b442d0b...). The second pass added exact_fix2.py for the per-step alias bounds of K57 and HF-N02, the K55 seam values at dx = 1/4, the HF-L02 falsifier factors and the cost sums (0ae9bc5ea85415ce..., output 5fb51e92efc01e79...). The third pass added exact_fix3.py for the top mode of the HF-N02 strip (K57), the 2nd-order miss of HF-N02, the reach of its alias bound past the stability edge and what the cost sum assumes (abad5b5fbe2bf1da..., output 0ca360d85e526459...). The fourth pass added exact_fix4.py for the HF-G12 (c) centre (gp1d.py's gap relaxation ported to integer fixed point at 2^64, as in exact_wet.py), the K62 numbers that HF-G07 quotes for a ramp-made event and the guard step counts of HF-N02 (0523094447950bad..., output 88a169f055f9c8c2...)|json=0
HFDEF|term=pins|meaning=this file is pinned by the sidecar PREDICTION-HELIUM-FILM.hbp.sha256, one GNU sha256sum line (64 hex digits, two spaces, PREDICTION-HELIUM-FILM.hbp) as the other .hbp sidecars of the repository, so sha256sum -c reads it (scripts/check-pins.sh group B; the freeze commit re-freezes B_FILES 2216 to 2217, B_FILES_ALL_OK 673 to 674, B_OK 691 to 692 before the run that measures them)|json=0
