CONST|id=K55|name=wall potential U_w(z; C3), z the exact signed distance to the union of solids (positive in the fluid), computed with isqrt at Q80|value=-C3/z^3 for z >= z_c = 5/2; -V0 = -C3/z_c^3 for 0 <= z < z_c; -V0 + (U_rep + V0)(3t^2 - 2t^3), t = min(1, -z/w), U_rep = 8, w = 1, for z < 0; linear in C3; baseline C3 = 32 (V0 = 256/125)|units=m c0^2|tag=DEFINED|source=lane 2 design; the nearest solid alone sets z, so the floor attracts the bath surface too (HF-G02 v)|verified=1|note=inside the solids z is minus the distance to the nearest fluid point; the minimum over solids of each solid's own signed distance is wrong there along internal seams (the G0 and G1 walls on the floor, the G2 cup floor on the plate), where at dx = 1/2 it gives z = -1/4 and U = 5/4 - (27/32) V0 = -239/500 at C3 = 32 and -1103/500 at C3 = 64, an attractive slot inside the solid (at dx = 1/4 the seam cells sit at z = -1/8, where U = 11/32 - (245/256) V0 = -1293/800 and -2861/800)|used_by=all HF-G rows|json=0
