CONST|id=K57|name=numerics|value=psi = (re, im) as i64 at 2^40, i128 products, round to nearest; 4th-order Laplacian (-1, 16, -30, 16, -1)/(12 dx^2) per axis; dx = 1/2 (checks 1/4); real-time RK4 dt = 1/64 (checks 1/128); imaginary-time RK4 dt = 1/32 (1/64 at dx = 1/4); records every 2 time units; the HF-N02 dispersion strip, besides its 2-unit records, evaluates its mode coefficients at every step (dt = 1/64) and records each sign change (the two straddling steps and their raw coefficients): its n = 82 mode has a period of 2.2180, so records every 2 would alias it to pi - 2.8328 = 0.3088 rad per time unit; one RK4 step multiplies a mode by R(iy), y = eps dt, and turns its phase by less than pi while y < sqrt6 (Im R(iy) = y (1 - y^2/6) > 0; R(i sqrt6) = -1/2 exactly), so per-step evaluation cannot alias a mode with eps below 64 sqrt6 = 156.7673; for 6 <= y^2 <= 8, up to the stability edge, Re R(iy) = 1 - y^2/2 + y^4/24 < 0, so an alias reads above 64 pi/2 = 100.531 rad per time unit (about 122.28 at the edge), far outside every band; the strip's modes lie below sqrt(4480/9) = 22.3109, because k dx = n pi/256 < pi on its mirrored x axis (the top one, n = 255 with ky dx = pi, is 22.3104; eps dt < 0.3487); mirror ghosts (2 cells) at x ends; Dirichlet at the top and deep in the floor core; sums in i128 in a fixed order|units=-|tag=DEFINED|source=lane 2 design (style of twens 0.4.0, qnn polariton-bridge/engines/ensemble)|verified=1|used_by=all HF-G, HF-N rows|json=0
CONST|id=K58|name=geometries (xi; solid floor y < 0; domain from y = -2)|value=strip: 2 cells x [0, 68]; G0: x [0, 144] mirrored, wall x [64, 80] to y = 160, cap radius 8 (top 168), level 32, y to 192, 288 x 388 sites; G0d: G0 with level 64 (y to 192); G1: x [0, 208], inner bath [0, 96], wall [96, 112] to y = 144, cap radius 8 (top 152), outer bath [112, 208], mean level 80, y to 176, 416 x 356 sites; G2: x [0, 96], cup floor x [0, 32] y [72, 80], plate x [32, 48] y [64, 168] with radius-8 semicircles (cap top 176, tip bottom 56), bath y [80, 104], pool level 16, y to 200, 192 x 404 sites; shelf: x [0, 128] mirrored, solid y < 0, g = 0, y to 26, 256 x 56 sites; box: 64 x 64 cells periodic in both directions, V = 0 (HF-N01); dispersion strip: 256 x 2 cells, x mirrored on [0, 128], y periodic, V = 0 (HF-N02); row1d, the 1D reduced row problem of HF-G02, HF-G12, HF-G13 and HF-G14: 88 cells at z = -4 + (i + 1/2)/2 from the solid face (z in [-4, 40]), the two outermost cells at each end are ghosts, held at zero at the solid end and at a vacuum far end (Dirichlet) and set to the last free cell before each step at a liquid far end (the HF-G12 gap rows), as in gp1d.py, and started as gp1d.py (phi the real field of imaginary time): a gap row from phi = 1 at z > 0 and 0 at z <= 0, a film row from phi = 1 on -1 < z < 10 (-1 < z < 12 at C3 = 64) and 0 elsewhere, and relaxed by imaginary-time RK4 at dt = 1/32 to tau = 2048 (65,536 steps; the frozen 1D values came from gp1d.py relaxed to tau = 800 by explicit Euler, and at h = 24 and 96 its tau = 1600 runs agree with them to every printed digit, extra.txt); wetting strip of HF-G11 (a): 68 cells, z in [-4, 30], zero ghosts at the solid end, a liquid far end, g = 0, mu = mu0, started from phi = 1 at z > 0 and 0 at z <= 0, as gp1d.py, and relaxed to tau = 600 (from a seed it would relax to the dry strip, HF-G11)|units=-|tag=DEFINED|source=lane 2 design; G0d, shelf and box added in this synthesis; row1d and the wetting strip frozen in the fix pass, their starts in the second pass, the row1d relaxation length in the third pass|verified=1|used_by=all HF-G, HF-N rows|json=0
