PREDICT|id=HF-S01|kind=REAL_HELIUM|tag=DERIVED|control=-|fixed_by_inputs=1|statement=Helium-4 atomic mass m4 = A_r m_u, liquid number density n = rho/m4 and interatomic spacing a = (m4/rho)^(1/3) at 1.3 K (SVP); the conventional 3.6 A atomic layer agrees with a within 1 percent.|predicted=m4 = 6.6464790808691923446396e-27 kg exactly; n in [2.183434e28, 2.183435e28] m^-3; a in [3.577832, 3.577833] A; abs(a/3.6 - 1) in [0.006157, 0.006158], <= 0.01|verdict_rule=MET if every certified interval lies inside its frozen band and abs(a/3.6 - 1) <= 0.01|method=method.statics; a by cube-root bracketing at a scale giving 1e-9 A|falsifier=a certified interval outside its band or abs(a/3.6 - 1) > 0.01 (NOT_MET); a re-read of NIST, CODATA or Donnelly-Barenghi that changes an input|inputs=K01, K02, K10, K38|cost=under 1 s|from=lane1:HF-S01 kept|json=0
PREDICT|id=HF-S02|kind=REAL_HELIUM|tag=DERIVED|control=-|fixed_by_inputs=1|statement=The one helium van der Waals constant of the study: the effective non-retarded film constant on polished metal back-solved from Ham and Jackson's d(1 cm) = 3.15e-6 cm at 2.05 K, C3_He = m4 g_n H d(H)^3 at H = 1 cm. Lane 3's value from a round 30 nm and the quartz thin-film alpha are not used anywhere.|predicted=C3_He = 2.03724837065e-50 J m^3 (exact rational, certified to 1e-60 J m^3) = 1475.5730 K A^3 (inside [1475.5729, 1475.5731]) = 127.15504 meV A^3 +/- 0.00001 = 31.62665 K (3.6 A layer)^3 +/- 0.00001|verdict_rule=MET if every certified value lies inside its band|method=method.statics; exact products, division by the exact k_B and e; no roots|falsifier=a certified value outside its band (NOT_MET); a re-read of Ham-Jackson k|inputs=K03, K04, K05, K07, K20, K38|cost=under 1 s|from=lane1:HF-S02 restated (quartz part removed; one C3 pinned study-wide, both judges)|json=0
PREDICT|id=HF-S03|kind=REAL_HELIUM|tag=DERIVED|control=-|fixed_by_inputs=1|statement=Receipt for the non-retarded profile d(h) = (C3_He/(m4 g_n h))^(1/3) = 315 A (1 cm/h)^(1/3). The 1 cm value is the anchor, so this row is not a test of the owner's 30 nm (HF-S04 is). Outside Ham-Jackson's measured 0.4 to 1.6 cm the values extrapolate a law whose exponent HF-S05 shows is not the measured one.|predicted=d(0.5 cm) = 396.8751, d(1) = 315.0000, d(2) = 250.0157, d(5) = 184.2131, d(10) = 146.2100 A, each +/- 0.0001|verdict_rule=MET if every certified interval lies inside its band|method=method.statics; cube-root bracketing of 315^3 10^(3s)/h|falsifier=a certified interval outside +/- 0.0001 A (NOT_MET)|inputs=K20, HF-S02|cost=under 1 s|from=lane1:HF-S03 restated as a receipt (both judges: circular as a test; quartz part removed)|json=0
PREDICT|id=HF-S04|kind=REAL_HELIUM|tag=CONJECTURE|control=-|fixed_by_inputs=1|statement=The literature does not fix d(1 cm) to 10 percent. Measured on metal: Ham-Jackson 1957 315 A (2.05 K, static optical); Grimes-Jackson 1959 320 A (2.04 K, UNVERIFIED); Kwoh 1979 335 +/- 10 A (stainless steel, a model-dependent fit of Atkins' oscillation theory); Keller 1970 460 to 480 A (stainless steel, as quoted by Kwoh). Claim 1: max/min of the measured values exceeds 1.10. Claim 2: Keller lies outside the owner's about-30-nm band [250, 350] A, the other three inside. Context, no verdict: Lifshitz theory with retardation gives 240 to 290 A on metals, below all three lower measurements.|predicted=max/min in [1.460317, 1.523810], > 1.10; HJ 315, GJ 320 and Kwoh [325, 345] inside [250, 350]; Keller [460, 480] outside|verdict_rule=MET if both claims hold on the certified rationals|method=method.statics; exact rational ratios, integer comparisons|falsifier=max/min <= 1.10 or a band membership other than the frozen one (NOT_MET); a read of the Keller 1970 or Grimes-Jackson 1959 primaries that changes an input|inputs=K20, K21, K22, K25, K26|cost=under 1 s|from=lane1:HF-S04 restated (Keller added, Kwoh model dependence stated; judge-lowT)|json=0
PREDICT|id=HF-S05|kind=REAL_HELIUM|tag=DERIVED|control=-|fixed_by_inputs=1|statement=Literature-exponent check, not a method control. At T = 2.05 K and z = 2.3, both frozen here as the deciding inputs, over Ham-Jackson's 0.4 <= H <= 1.6 cm the pure non-retarded exponent 1/3 deviates from their fitted law d = 3.15e-6 cm H^(-1/z) (same 1 cm anchor) by more than 5 percent somewhere; NR/HJ = H^(7/69) is monotone, so the endpoints bound it. Information only, no verdict: z of about 2.6 at 1.32 K gives 4.590 percent (under 5), and the Anderson-Liebenberg-Dillinger thicknesses give an exponent 0.2822, on the other side of 1/3: the measured exponent is not one constant.|predicted=NR/HJ(0.4 cm) in [0.911232, 0.911233]; NR/HJ(1.6 cm) in [1.048836, 1.048837]; maximum deviation in [8.8767, 8.8768] percent, > 5|verdict_rule=MET if the certified maximum deviation exceeds 5 percent and the intervals lie in their bands|method=method.statics; (2/5)^7 and (8/5)^7, then the 69th root by integer bracketing|falsifier=certified maximum deviation <= 5 percent (NOT_MET); a re-read of Ham-Jackson's z at 2.05 K|inputs=K20, K32|cost=under 1 s|from=lane1:HF-S05 restated (relabelled; it is not one of the negative controls; both judges)|json=0
PREDICT|id=HF-S07|kind=REAL_HELIUM|tag=CONJECTURE|control=-|fixed_by_inputs=1|statement=Three routes to the film critical velocity at thickness d: v_rate = sigma/((rho_s/rho) d), v_PA = hbar/(2 m4 d) (Pickar-Atkins) and v_vA = Gamma d^(-1/4) (van Alphen, UNVERIFIED, measured in channels). They are not independent: v_rate/v_PA does not depend on d, and only v_vA/v_PA = (d/d*)^(3/4) tests the thickness (HF-S12). Claim 1: the d-independent identity for Daunt-Mendelssohn's rate at 1.3 K. Claim 2: v_PA and v_vA lie in the owner's 20 to 30 cm/s band at 315 and 335 A, but v_PA does not at Keller's 470 A. Agreement of these routes is dimensional, not a validation (HF-L04).|predicted=v_rate/v_PA = 0.989927 +/- 0.000001 at every d (sigma 7.5e-5 cm^2/s, rho_s/rho 0.955); at 315 A v_PA = 25.18512, v_vA = 23.73681, v_rate = 24.93144 cm/s; at 335 A v_PA = 23.68153, v_vA = 23.37431 cm/s; at 470 A v_PA = 16.87939 cm/s (below 20) and v_vA = 21.47709 cm/s; each velocity +/- 0.00001|verdict_rule=MET if every certified value lies in its band and every band membership holds as stated|method=method.statics; hbar from h and the rational pi bracket; 4th-root bracketing for v_vA|falsifier=a certified value outside its band or a membership flip (NOT_MET); a primary read of Daunt-Mendelssohn 1939 or van Alphen 1966 that changes an input|inputs=K03, K06, K08, K12, K20, K22, K25, K27, K30, K31|cost=under 1 s|from=lane1:HF-S07 restated (not independent routes, carry the spread; both judges); absorbs HF-S08 and HF-S09|json=0
PREDICT|id=HF-S10|kind=REAL_HELIUM|tag=CONJECTURE|control=-|fixed_by_inputs=1|statement=Drain time of a stated beaker: thin-walled glass, inner radius r = 1.000 cm, liquid depth 2.000 cm, rim 1.000 cm above the liquid at the start, hung above the bath, rho_s/rho = 0.955 (1.3 K). The rim perimeter 2 pi r is the bottleneck; evaporation, film start-up and the outside wall are neglected; h is the rim height above the inside level (1 to 3 cm), Q = 2 pi r sigma(h), t = integral of r dh/(2 sigma). Models: (a) Pickar-Atkins, sigma = (rho_s/rho) hbar/(2 m4), independent of d, h and Kontorovich thinning (Daunt-Mendelssohn's height independence); (b) van Alphen on the static film d = 315 A (1 cm/h)^(1/3), sigma = (rho_s/rho) Gamma d^(3/4); (c) as (b) on the Kontorovich-thinned film C3_He/(m4 d^3) = g_n h + (rho_s/rho) v^2/2, v = Gamma d^(-1/4); (DM) the glass rate 7.5e-5, constant. Measured-rate band [5.0e-5, 11.7e-5] from Seki's zero-head rate to Kwoh's stainless-steel rate plus its spread; rates are cell and substrate specific. Claim: every model time lies inside the measured-rate band of times. This is the owner's perimeter x thickness x critical velocity; lane 1's HF-S09 rim flux is folded in.|predicted=(a) sigma = 7.576313e-5 cm^2/s, Q = 4.760338e-4 cm^3/s (mass rate 6.908273e-5 g/s at 0.1451215 g/cm^3), t_a = 13199.033 s (3.666398 h); (b) Q(start) = 4.486588e-4 cm^3/s, t_b = 16515.202 s; (c) rim thinning d_flow/d_static = 0.919551 at h = 1 cm (0.952339 at 2 cm, 0.965296 at 3 cm), Q(start) = 4.213063e-4 cm^3/s, t_c in [17160.2, 17162.3] s, t_c/t_a in [1.3001, 1.3003]; (DM) t = 40000/3 s = 13333.333 s exactly; measured-rate band of times [8547.009, 20000.000] s (Kwoh's 11.2e-5 alone 8928.571 s); each value +/- 1 in its last digit unless an interval is given|verdict_rule=MET if every certified value lies inside its band and t_a, t_b, t_c and t_DM all lie inside [8547.009, 20000.000] s|method=method.statics; pi cancels (perimeter over area); 4th-root and cube-root bracketing; for (c) d = w^4 turns the Kontorovich equation into the monotone polynomial g_n h w^12 + (rho_s/rho)(Gamma^2/2) w^10 = C3_He/m4, solved by integer bisection on w with no root extraction, and sigma = (rho_s/rho) Gamma w^3; the integral bracketed by lower and upper Riemann sums of the monotone integrand on 2^16 panels (the bracket is at most 0.0613 s wide; for Gamma = 1 the closed form t_c = G(w(1 cm)) - G(w(3 cm)), G(w) = w^-5/(10 g_n) - 2 C3_He w^-15/(5 m4 g_n (rho_s/rho)), gives [17161.2094, 17161.2095] s, so the 2^16-panel bracket lies in [17161.1482, 17161.2708] s, inside the band; exact_extra.py)|falsifier=a value outside its band or a model time outside the measured band (NOT_MET); physically, a measured drain time at 1.3 K for this geometry outside [8547, 20000] s would falsify every model (no such measurement was found)|inputs=K03, K04, K06, K08, K10, K12, K20, K23, K24, K27, K28, K30, K31|cost=seconds (2^16 + 1 polynomial bisections on w; d = w^4 removes the 4th root at every panel)|from=lane1:HF-S10 restated (Kontorovich-thinned rim, laws named, glass-specific rate, Kwoh as physical falsifier, HF-S09 folded in; both judges)|json=0
PREDICT|id=HF-S12|kind=REAL_HELIUM|tag=CONJECTURE|control=-|fixed_by_inputs=1|statement=The Pickar-Atkins and van Alphen laws cross at d* = (hbar/(2 m4 Gamma))^(4/3). Claim: d* lies inside the 1 cm thickness band [250, 350] A, and the laws agree within 10 percent only for d in [d* 1.1^(-4/3), d* 0.9^(-4/3)]. Agreement within 10 percent means the ratio v_PA/v_vA = (d*/d)^(3/4) lies in [0.9, 1.1]. Every remaining comparison of lane 1's HF-S08 and HF-S09 is a function of d/d* and lives here.|predicted=d* = 340.8835 A (inside [340.8835, 340.8836]); 10 percent window [300.2035, 392.2979] A, each +/- 0.0001; information only, no verdict: the reverse ratio v_vA/v_PA in [0.9, 1.1] would give [296.2074, 387.0761] A; d* sits at a film height of 0.789066 cm on the h^(-1/3) law|verdict_rule=MET if d* lies in [250, 350] A and the certified values in their bands|method=method.statics; cube root of the 4th power by integer bracketing (the window edges as cube roots of d*^3 1.1^-4 and d*^3 0.9^-4)|falsifier=d* outside [250, 350] A (NOT_MET), as for Gamma = 0.9 instead of 1; a primary read of van Alphen 1966|inputs=K03, K06, K08, K20, K30, K31|cost=under 1 s|from=lane1:HF-S12 kept (Gamma marked UNVERIFIED, so CONJECTURE)|json=0
PREDICT|id=HF-S14|kind=REAL_HELIUM|tag=DERIVED|control=-|fixed_by_inputs=1|statement=The low-temperature saturated-film transfer rate is not one literature constant: Seki 1962's zero-head rate (5e-5, which Seki calls the true critical rate) and Kwoh 1979's stainless-steel rate (11.2 +/- 0.5e-5 at about 1.4 K) differ by more than a factor 2. In units of hbar/(2 m4), the Pickar-Atkins rate before its rho_s/rho factor, the Pickar-Atkins value rho_s/rho (0.955 at 1.3 K, 0.966 at 1.25 K) lies inside the span of the two. Context, no verdict: Seki's normally observed 8e-5 (1.008406 in these units) and Daunt-Mendelssohn's 7.5e-5 (glass, UNVERIFIED; 0.945381) lie between. Lane 1's +/- 15 percent consistency claim would be NOT_MET and is withdrawn.|predicted=Kwoh/Seki_zero_head in [2.14, 2.34], > 2; rates over hbar/(2 m4): Seki zero head 0.630254, Kwoh [1.348743, 1.474794], each +/- 0.000001, so 0.955 and 0.966 lie inside; hbar/(2 m4) = 7.933312e-5 cm^2/s|verdict_rule=MET if the certified ratio interval lies above 2 and the listed values lie in their bands|method=method.statics; exact rational ratios|falsifier=certified ratio <= 2 (NOT_MET); a re-read of Seki 1962 or Kwoh 1979|inputs=K03, K06, K08, K12, K23, K28 (context, no verdict: K27, K29)|cost=under 1 s|from=lane1:HF-S14 restated (Kwoh and Seki zero-head rates added; both judges)|json=0
PREDICT|id=HF-G01|kind=MODEL_EXACT|tag=CONJECTURE|control=-|fixed_by_inputs=0|statement=Imaginary time at fixed mu = mu0 = -1/2 on the 1D strip (2-cell mirrored column, y in [0, 68], mirror at y = 0, Dirichlet at the top, step start at y = 34) relaxes the liquid-vacuum interface to the model's exact solution rho(y) = 1/(1 + exp(2(y - y_m))) with bulk rho = 1 and sigma = 1/4. The solution is DERIVED (K53); the bands are estimates.|predicted=dx = 1/2: max abs(rho_num - rho_exact) <= 0.01 (design 0.0022, aligned at the measured midpoint y_m); abs(sigma_num/0.25 - 1) <= 0.01; bulk abs(rho - 1) <= 1e-9; dx = 1/4: max error <= 0.001 (design 0.00026); err(1/2)/err(1/4) >= 6 (design 8.43; a 2nd-order stencil gives about 4)|verdict_rule=MET if every bound holds|method=method.gp; imaginary-time RK4, dt = 1/32 (dx 1/2) and 1/64 (dx 1/4), tau = 128; midpoint by linear interpolation; sigma_num = sum of [discrete energy density - mu0 rho] dy with the kinetic term consistent with the stencil; exact exp values from certified integer Taylor bounds|falsifier=any bound exceeded (NOT_MET)|inputs=K50, K51, K52, K53, K57, K58|cost=two runs under 1 s each|from=L2-GP-01 kept, retagged CONJECTURE (judge-lowT); convergence bound repaired from >= 8 to >= 6 (synthesis design check: the midpoint alignment is not 4th order)|json=0
PREDICT|id=HF-G02|kind=MODEL_EXACT|tag=CONJECTURE|control=-|fixed_by_inputs=0|statement=Film statics in G0, grand-canonical imaginary time at mu = mu0 + 32 g (y_L* = 32). On both faces the equilibrium thickness s(h) (outermost downward rho = 1/2 crossing along a row, from the exact solid surface, h = y - 32) matches the 1D reduced solution of the same row problem. The TF law (8192/h)^(1/3) holds only asymptotically: the finite interface width adds +3 to +5 percent (referee), so lane 2's 3 percent band about s_TF is withdrawn. h = 128 meets the cap junction and gets no verdict. The GP film is 4 to 7 xi thick, not 30 nm (HF-L01).|predicted=(i) s(24, 32, 48, 64, 96) = 7.1935, 6.5665, 5.7725, 5.2678, 4.6346 xi (1D reduced, engine discretization), G0 within 1.5 percent of each; s/s_TF - 1 = +2.9, +3.4, +4.1, +4.5, +5.3 percent. (ii) least-squares slope of ln s on ln h over those heights -0.3173 +/- 0.010 (TF -1/3). (iii) thin-seed and thick-slab starts agree within 0.02 xi at every height; dx = 1/4 agrees with dx = 1/2 within 0.03 xi. (iv) coverage (rho summed over cells at signed distance >= 0, per unit height) over n0 s: 1.435 at h = 24 and 1.514 at h = 96, +/- 0.05; share of that coverage in the capped wall layer 0 <= z < 2.5: 0.437 and 0.609, +/- 0.05 (the film is a dense slab, rho about 1.8 at the wall, not helium's rho d; this replaces lane 3's L3-13, whose premise is reversed in this model). (v) bath rho = 1/2 surface at the mirror axis x = 0: 32.244 +/- 0.05 xi (lane 2's 32 omitted the floor's own attraction: y_s - 32 = 8192/y_s^3 gives 32.2444)|verdict_rule=MET if (i) to (v) all hold|method=method.gp; G0 at dx = 1/2, imaginary-time RK4 dt = 1/32, tau = 2048 (slowest mode, the bath level, has time constant 128); starts (a) bath rho = 1 below y = 32 plus a uniform seed 2^-20, (b) the same plus a 12 xi slab on every solid face; one dx = 1/4 run (dt = 1/64); the engine's 1D row mode computes the reduced solution and must reproduce the frozen 1D values within 0.1 percent; slope by exact rational least squares on certified integer logarithms; the 1D values are row1d solutions (K58: z in [-4, 40], Dirichlet, as in gp1d.py); every named height is a cell edge, so s, the coverage and the wall-layer share at each h are the means over the two straddling rows (cell.edge), compared with the 1D values at the exact h; the axis level (v) is read on the first column (cell.edge)|falsifier=any band missed (NOT_MET); in particular the two starts differing by more than 0.02 xi (no unique equilibrium)|inputs=K50 to K58|cost=G0 dx 1/2: 111,744 sites, 65,536 steps, 2 to 4 min per start on 4 CPUs, about 10 MB; dx 1/4: 446,976 sites, 131,072 steps, 16 to 32 min (8 times the dx 1/2 run: 4 times the sites, 2 times the steps), about 40 MB|from=L2-GP-02 restated (re-toleranced against the 1D reduced solution, h = 128 dropped from the verdict; referee point 2, judge-lowT); axis level repaired in this synthesis|json=0
PREDICT|id=HF-G03|kind=MODEL_EXACT|tag=CONJECTURE|control=NEGATIVE|fixed_by_inputs=0|statement=With the wall attraction off (C3 = 0 on every solid, repulsive core kept) there is no film: attraction to the wall stronger than to the liquid itself is what makes it. (a) G0 imaginary-time equilibrium: no film on either face and a depressed meniscus, with contact angle 180 degrees. This is exact in the continuum: for U_w >= 0, as at C3 = 0, the Bogomolny bound (1/2) phi'^2 + (rho/2)(rho - 1)^2 >= abs(phi') phi abs(1 - rho), with rho = phi^2, integrates over the rise from the wall to the bulk to sigma_wl >= 1/4 = sigma_lv. The draft design value 0.2489 came from an np.diff kinetic term and is a discretization artifact. The frozen wetting strip of HF-G11 (a), with the stencil-consistent kinetic term, gives +0.2501 at tau = 600; it drifts toward the discrete free-surface value 0.24992 (dx = 1/2) as the free interface leaves the repulsive wall. Part (a) is the negative control. (b) is a bug check, not a physical control. G2 is prepared as D2 (mu_in = mu0 + 104 g in the cup, mu_out = mu0 + 16 g outside, barrier on, then ramped off over 64) but with C3 = 0, then run in real time for 2000 in the frame at (mu_in + mu_out)/2, so both baths' phases rotate and every integrator stage does nonzero work. At C3 = 0 the baths are disconnected and each starts from its own equilibrium, so the drive moves no mass in the model; (b) can fail only through a code fault, such as a wrong sign, a stencil that couples across the empty plate, or a mass leak.|predicted=(a) on every row with h >= 24: max rho within 10 xi of either face <= 1e-6 (exact Q40 zero above about h = 30); the bath rho = 1/2 surface 3 xi from each face (the columns x = 61 and x = 83, each the mean of its two straddling columns, cell.edge) lies at least 2 xi below y_L* = 32. (b) bug check: M_face_out (rho dx^2 summed over x >= 40, y >= 72) = 0 as an exact integer at every record; no cell with rho > 0 at y >= 140 inside the cup at any record; N(t) within HF-G04's D2 bound|verdict_rule=MET if every claim holds|method=method.gp; G0 imaginary time as HF-G02 with C3 = 0; G2 preparation and real-time RK4 dt = 1/64 as HF-G09 with C3 = 0|falsifier=any nonzero film mass or a meniscus at or above y_L* - 2 in (a) (NOT_MET: the film would not come from the wall attraction alone); any nonzero outer-face mass in (b) (NOT_MET: a code fault)|inputs=K53, K55, K57, K58, K59|cost=G0 about 3 min; G2 77,568 sites, 128,000 steps, 6 to 9 min plus 1 to 2 min preparation|from=L2-GP-03 merged with L3-01 (control run under D2's drive; both judges); in the fix pass (b) is labelled a bug check and the 180-degree angle is tied to the Bogomolny bound (final critic)|json=0
PREDICT|id=HF-G04|kind=NUMERICS|tag=CONJECTURE|control=-|fixed_by_inputs=0|statement=Fixed-point RK4 at Q40 conserves the discrete norm N = sum rho dx^2 and energy E (kinetic term with the same stencil as the right-hand side, exact i128 sums) to the stated bounds over every real-time run after its last time-dependent input (t0 = 64 after the barrier ramp; t0 = 128 after the C3 ramp of HF-G08), and halving dt does not move the observables.|predicted=abs(N/N(t0) - 1) and abs(E - E(t0))/N(t0) <= 1e-8 for U0, U8, U16; <= 1e-5 for U32 to U96, D2, the C3 = 0 control, the shelf run and the dispersion strip; D1r: N within 1e-5 throughout, E within 1e-5 after t0 = 128. U8 at dt = 1/128 against dt = 1/64 over 0.75 T: max over records abs(delta M_in) <= 1e-4 A_M (A_M = W u0/2 = 384 xi^2 n0); max abs(O_dt - O_dt/2)/range(O) <= 1e-3 for M_in, Gamma_top and q; per record abs(E_dt - E_dt/2)/N <= 1e-5 and abs(N_dt - N_dt/2)/N <= 1e-5. The lowest dissipative rung of HF-G07 at dt = 1/128: the time of its first counted event (HF-G07: the first record at t >= 64 with V > 0, or a valid record with N_slip != 0) within max(1 percent, 4 time units) of the dt = 1/64 run. If HF-G07 has no dissipative rung, there is no rung to rerun, so this timing part is not run and the row reads NOT_MET (HFDEF verdict).|verdict_rule=MET if every bound holds at every record|method=method.gp; N and E recorded every 2 time units as exact integer sums in a fixed reduction order (bit-identical for any thread count); reruns at dtden doubled|falsifier=any bound exceeded (NOT_MET); a first-order slip in a stage would show in the dt/2 comparison; no dissipative rung in HF-G07, so the dt/2 timing part is not run (NOT_MET)|inputs=K57, K60, K65|cost=U8 at dt/2: 288,000 steps on 148,096 sites, 21 to 31 min; the dissipative rung at dt/2: 288,000 steps, 21 to 31 min|from=L2-GP-04 merged with L3-06 (a), (b), (d); L3-06 (c), the order ratio R, dropped (rounding-limited, no verdict defined; referee); D1 bound restated for the ramp; the first-event time limited to records at t >= 64 in the second pass (verification); the timing part with no dissipative rung stated in the fourth pass (verification)|json=0
PREDICT|id=HF-G05|kind=MECHANISM|tag=CONJECTURE|control=-|fixed_by_inputs=0|statement=Frictionless film transfer below a critical speed, the GP analog of Atkins' film oscillations (period and rate are the model's, not helium's). G1: a wall in a bath, baths 96 xi wide, mean level 80, rim cap top 72 xi above it. Released from a level difference u0 = 8 or 16 by ramping the rim barrier down over 64, the film carries mass over the rim back and forth without vortices; period and rate follow the reduced inertial model (K62). Two sub-claims added: Kontorovich thinning of the flowing film at the rim (the counterpart of Kwoh's observation, at twice the flow frequency) and the share of the dense superfluid wall layer, which in helium is solid (K39). The release is not exactly from rest. In the frame at (mu_in + mu_out)/2 the two bath phases drift apart at the rate g u0 while the barrier ramps down, so the junction opens near t = 64 with a phase difference of about g u0 t = u0/4: 2 rad for U8 and 4 rad for U16. That imprints an initial current. In the higher rungs of HF-G07 (8 rad for U32, 24 rad for U96) it can drive Josephson slips during the ramp. No verdict counts a record before t = 64 (K61), but a vortex present at t = 64 or later counts, whatever made it.|predicted=(i) V(t) = 0 at every record with 64 <= t <= 4500, and N_slip = 0 at every valid record (K61, referenced at t_ref, the first valid record at t >= 64); (ii) S2 = swing2/swing1 >= 0.95; (iii) half-period (t = 0 to the first minimum of M_in) 1501 +/- 25 percent, in [1126, 1876]; (iv) q_max/u0 in [0.075, 0.126]; (v) dx = 1/4 rerun of U8 for 4096 time units (262,144 steps), long enough to reach t_max2 even at the top of the half-period band with the 3 percent allowance (2 x 1.03 x 1876 + 32 = 3896.56 < 4096; 0.75 T = 2250 would not reach it, and 3400 would reach it only for half-periods up to 1684 without the allowance and 1634.95 with it): half-period within 3 percent and S2 within 0.02 of dx = 1/2; (vi) U16: delta_K = 1 - Gamma_top(t_q)/[(Gamma_top(t_min1) + Gamma_top(t_max2))/2] in [0.010, 0.060], with t_min1, t_max2 the first minimum and the next maximum of M_in and t_q the record of largest abs(q) between them, and delta_K/(0.476 v_q^2) in [0.5, 1.5] with v_q = q/Gamma_top at t_q (design 0.026 from the 1D coverage slope at h = 72); (vii) the wall-layer share of Gamma_top (cells at signed distance [0, 2.5) from the cap over all column cells) in [0.45, 0.70] at every record after t = 64 (1D design 0.55); its flux share is reported without a verdict|verdict_rule=MET if (i) to (vii) all hold|method=method.gp; imaginary-time preparation with mu_in = mu0 + g(80 + u0/2) for x < 104 and mu_out = mu0 + g(80 - u0/2), barrier on; then real-time RK4 dt = 1/64 in the frame at (mu_in + mu_out)/2 for 4500 (the dx = 1/4 rerun for 4096); Gamma_top = the sum of rho dy over the cells of the cap-top column x = 104 at signed distance >= 0, and its wall-layer part over [0, 2.5); x = 104 is a cell edge, so both are the means over the two straddling columns (cell.edge); records M_in, M_out, Gamma_top and its wall-layer part, q(t) = (M_in(t - 2) - M_in(t + 2))/4 (defined only on records with 2 <= t <= t_end - 2, which have both neighbours; t_end = 4500, or 4096 in the dx = 1/4 rerun; q_max, t_q and v_q are read on those records only), V(t), N_slip(t); swing1 = M_in(0) - M_in(t_min1), swing2 = M_in(t_max2) - M_in(t_min1)|falsifier=a counted vortex or slip at t >= 64; S2 < 0.95; half-period outside [1126, 1876]; q_max/u0 outside [0.075, 0.126]; the dx check failing; delta_K or the wall share out of band (NOT_MET)|inputs=K24, K54 to K62, K64 (background only, no verdict: K39)|cost=per run 148,096 sites, 288,000 steps, 21 to 31 min, about 15 MB, plus 3 to 5 min preparation; dx = 1/4: 592,384 sites, 262,144 steps, about 82 to 119 min plus 24 to 40 min preparation (8 times the dx 1/2 preparation: 4 times the sites, 2 times the imaginary-time steps)|from=L2-GP-05 kept with Kontorovich (judge-lowT) and wall-layer share (judge-lowT) sub-claims; in the fix pass the dx = 1/4 rerun runs 4096 time units and slips count from t_ref (final critic); the records on which q is defined stated in the fourth pass (verification)|json=0
PREDICT|id=HF-G06|kind=MECHANISM|tag=CONJECTURE|control=-|fixed_by_inputs=0|statement=Below the critical drive the peak transfer rate grows linearly with the head; above it, phase slips limit the flow. A van der Waals film in Bernoulli balance has Fr^2 < 2/3 and a flux that rises monotonically with speed (K64), so no hydraulic choke limits it, and thinning alone would raise the rim speed with drive. This is the GP analog of the Daunt-Mendelssohn head independence; helium's rate, which is not exactly head independent (Seki), is not predicted.|predicted=(i) q_max(U16)/q_max(U8) in [1.9, 2.1]; (ii) rim-speed plateau over the first forward swing (t from 64 to the first sign change of q after its first extremum, or 2250): v_rim,max(U96)/v_rim,max(U80) in [0.85, 1.10], where frictionless flow would give at least 1.2; (iii) N_slip = 0 at every valid record of U0, U8 and U16 (K61: records at t >= 64, referenced at t_ref); for U80 and U96, read at the last valid record at or before t = 2250 of each run: N_slip >= 5 in both, and N_slip(U96) > N_slip(U80) (Josephson-Anderson: the slip rate follows g u/(2 pi); design about 20 and 30)|verdict_rule=MET if (i) to (iii) all hold|method=method.gp; rungs U80 and U96 (u0 = 80 and 96) run for 2250 = 0.75 T, plus U0, U8 and U16; v_rim = q/Gamma_top; N_slip by the K61 counter|falsifier=a ratio outside its band; a slip in a subcritical rung; fewer than 5 slips in U80 or U96 or no increase with drive (NOT_MET)|inputs=K59 to K62, K64|cost=2 runs of 144,000 steps, 11 to 16 min each|from=L2-GP-06 restated: plateau speeds q/Gamma_top over the first forward swing (judge-lowT) and the Josephson-Anderson slip count (referee) replace the plateau-flux ratio; (iii) read at the last valid record at or before t = 2250 in the second pass (verification)|json=0
PREDICT|id=HF-G07|kind=MECHANISM|tag=CONJECTURE|control=-|fixed_by_inputs=0|statement=Onset of dissipation on the drive ladder u0 = 0, 8, 16, 32, 48, 64, 80, 96, ordered by drive (not by measured speed, which slips clamp near v*). A rung is dissipative if any record at t >= 64 has V > 0 or N_slip != 0 (K61). The release is not from rest (HF-G05): the junction opens with a phase difference of about u0/4 rad, and in the higher rungs the ramp can drive slips. A slip completed before t_ref is not counted, because N_slip is referenced at t_ref (K61). A vortex present at any record at t >= 64 counts, whatever made it, so a vortex the ramp made that is still in the film at t = 64 makes the rung dissipative. The onset speed is in units of c_loc = c0 = 1, the sound speed of the uncompressed liquid on the free-surface side; the dense wall layer (rho about 1.8, c about 2.5) carries about half the flow (HF-G05 vii). Anchors, no verdict: Feynman's estimate about 0.47 (formula UNVERIFIED), the ripplon Landau speed mapped to the coverage-mean speed about 0.8, the transonic Mc = 0.4286 for a disc (Huepe-Brachet 1997). The crossover is the model's, not helium's critical velocity.|predicted=the dissipative rungs form an upper set in u0; at least one non-dissipative and one dissipative rung; v_rim = q/Gamma_top (HF-G05, HF-G06), and the v_rim,max of a rung is the largest v_rim over its records with 64 <= t <= t_end - 2, where q is defined (t_end the run's last record, HFDEF method.gp; during the ramp the K59 barrier sits on the cap-top column x = 104, where Gamma_top is read, and suppresses it, so earlier records do not count; HF-G06 ii reads its plateau over the first forward swing, which also starts at t = 64); the first counted event of a rung is its first record at t >= 64 with V > 0, or its first valid record (K61) with N_slip != 0; v_lo = the largest v_rim,max over non-dissipative rungs and v_hi = v_rim at the last record with t >= 64 before the first counted event of the lowest dissipative rung satisfy 0.35 <= v_lo <= v_hi <= 0.95; the two rungs that bracket onset, rerun at dx = 1/4, keep their classification, with v_hi(dx 1/4)/v_hi(dx 1/2) in [0.9, 1.1] (v_hi(dx 1/4) read the same way in the dx = 1/4 rerun of the lowest dissipative rung); if exactly one of the two runs whose v_hi is read (the dx = 1/2 run and the dx = 1/4 rerun of the lowest dissipative rung) has its first counted event at the record t = 64 and the other has its first counted event more than 4 time units later (after t = 68; the tolerance of HF-G04's dt/2 timing at t = 64), the dx check fails (NOT_MET); precondition (HFDEF verdict), for the remaining cases only: if a run whose v_hi is read has its first counted event at the record t = 64, that v_hi has no value, the claims that use it are not evaluated, and the row reads INCONCLUSIVE with that precondition printed, unless another claim fails (then NOT_MET); 0.35 <= v_lo <= 0.95 is checked in every case; the precondition covers only a first counted event at the record t = 64: a ramp-made event first counted later in the lowest dissipative rung (its dx = 1/2 run) reads NOT_MET, because v_hi is then read on the release transient (K62: in U48, v_rim is about 0.1 at t = 66 and stays below 0.35 until about t = 248), and a ramp-made event that makes U32 dissipative reads NOT_MET, because v_lo is then U16's v_rim,max, about 0.235 (K62), below 0.35; the empty case is a foreseeable outcome, not a surprise: in the higher rungs the ramp can drive slips (the junction opens with 8 rad in U32 and 12 rad in U48, more than one 2 pi turn), a vortex takes about 10 time units to cross the film, and onset is expected between U32 and U48, so a vortex the ramp made may still be in the film at t = 64 in the lowest dissipative rung, and an INCONCLUSIVE or a NOT_MET read is foreseen; expected v* about 0.6, onset between U32 and U48|verdict_rule=MET if every claim holds|method=method.gp; rungs U0 and U32 to U96 run for 0.75 T, U8 and U16 from HF-G05; detectors K60 and K61; records every 2 time units (a vortex takes about 10 to cross a 5 xi film)|falsifier=a non-monotone ladder; no bracket; v_lo < 0.35, v_lo > 0.95, v_hi > 0.95 or v_lo > v_hi; the dx = 1/4 reruns changing a classification or moving v_hi by more than 10 percent; exactly one of the two runs of the lowest dissipative rung with its first counted event at t = 64 while the other's comes after t = 68 (NOT_MET)|inputs=K52, K59 to K62 (anchors only, no verdict: K36, K37)|cost=6 runs of 144,000 steps (11 to 16 min each) plus 6 preparations (3 to 5 min each); 2 dx = 1/4 reruns of 2250 time units (45 to 65 min each, plus 24 to 40 min preparation each)|from=L2-GP-07 restated: ordered by drive with a measured bracket (judge-lowT) and a dx = 1/4 rerun of the bracketing rungs (referee); classification on records at t >= 64 in the fix pass (final critic); v_hi read on records at t >= 64, with its empty case named, in the second pass (verification); v_rim,max read on records at t >= 64, and the empty case kept out of the dx check unless the other run's first counted event comes by t = 68, in the third pass (verification); what the precondition does not cover (a ramp-made event first counted after t = 64, or one that makes U32 dissipative, reads NOT_MET) and the records on which q is defined stated in the fourth pass (verification)|json=0
PREDICT|id=HF-G08|kind=MECHANISM|tag=CONJECTURE|control=-|fixed_by_inputs=0|statement=Film formation and climbing in G2 (cup with a skirt tip above a collector; inner level y_L = 104, rim cap top 72 higher, tip bottom y = 56, pool level 16). Run D1r starts from the C3 = 0 equilibrium (dry wall, depressed meniscus) and ramps C3 linearly from 0 to 32 over 128 time units, 4 times the cup's sound-crossing time of about 32 (lane 2's sudden switch-on was a quench and is withdrawn). The film forms on the inner face, climbs it, crosses the rim and reaches the outer face. Expected order of events from the 1D design, no verdict (t = 4 C3 during the ramp): complete wetting from C3 about 2.83 (t about 11); a film stable at h = 24 from C3 about 5.2 (t about 21); the dry wall linearly unstable at coexistence from C3 = 11.64 (t about 47) and at h = 48 from C3 = 14.84 (t about 59). There the lowest bound state of -(1/2) d^2/dz^2 + U_w reaches mu0 - g h (-1/2 and -0.6875); these are exact inertia counts on the row1d discretization, and the dx = 1/20 2nd-order operator gives 11.55 and 14.73. At C3 = 10.7 the lowest bound state is -0.4459 (-0.4510 at dx = 1/20), above mu0 = -1/2, so the dry wall is still stable there even at coexistence. The draft value 10.7 (t about 43) came from the well-depth test V0 > 1/2 + g h, which ignores confinement, and is withdrawn.|predicted=the film front (the highest row y <= 168 with max rho >= 1/2 among the cells x in [22, 32)) passes y = 152 (h = 48) before t = 600; M_face_out > 1 xi^2 n0 before t = 1200|verdict_rule=MET if both times are met|method=method.gp; G2 real-time RK4 dt = 1/64 for 1600 from the C3 = 0 imaginary-time state prepared like D2 (mu_in = mu0 + 104 g, mu_out = mu0 + 16 g) but without the barrier (at C3 = 0 the baths are disconnected), frame at (mu_in + mu_out)/2; the wall table is core + (k/8192)(U(32) - core) at step k <= 8192 (U_w is linear in C3); front and M_face_out every 2 time units|falsifier=front below y = 152 at t = 600, or M_face_out <= 1 at t = 1200 (NOT_MET)|inputs=K55, K57, K58|cost=77,568 sites, 102,400 steps, 5 to 8 min, about 8 MB, plus 1 to 2 min preparation|from=L2-GP-08 restated with a C3 ramp (judge-lowT)|json=0
PREDICT|id=HF-G09|kind=MECHANISM|tag=CONJECTURE|control=-|fixed_by_inputs=0|statement=Dripping in the 2D cross-section. A 2D drop is a cylinder along the rim, so the size law is the model's 2D Tate law, not helium's drop size. G2 run D2: imaginary time with mu_in = mu0 + 104 g inside the cup and mu_out = mu0 + 16 g outside, barrier on the cap, then the barrier ramped off over 64. The film drains the cup over the rim and down the outer face, and liquid leaves the skirt tip as detached drops.|predicted=Definitions: a free component is a 4-connected component of cells with rho >= 1/2 that is connected neither to the film on the solid nor to the pool, that is, it contains no cell at signed distance below 2.5 from any solid (the pool lies on the floor, so this excludes it too); a drop is a free component whose area (cell count x dx^2) is at least 16 xi^2 when it is first detected. Free components are tracked from record to record: a free component continues the free component of the previous record with which it shares the most cells (ties: the one whose first cell in row-major order, by row j and then column i, comes first), and a free component that shares no cell with a free component of the previous record is new. When several free components would continue the same previous one, only the one that shares the most cells with it continues it (ties as above), and the others are new. The pinch-off point of a drop is its centroid (the mean of its cell centres, an exact rational) at the first record at which it is free, and its area is taken at that record. A drop is counted when its tracked centroid crosses y = 40 downward: centroid y >= 40 at one record and y < 40 at the next, free at both; each drop is counted at most once. Claims: at least 3 counted drops by t = 2000; the first drop (the earliest detected; two drops first detected at the same record are ordered by their first cell in row-major order) pinches off at y in [40, 56] with abs(x - 40) <= 12; the mean area at first detection of the counted drops in [40, 160] xi^2 (A_T = 128); the mass budget pool + films + cup = N(t0) within HF-G04's bound|verdict_rule=MET if every claim holds|method=method.gp; G2 real-time RK4 dt = 1/64 for 2000; every 2 time units an integer flood fill labels the components of rho >= 1/2, marks the free ones and tracks them by shared cells; centroids and areas as exact rationals|falsifier=fewer than 3 counted drops (for example a continuous curtain from tip to pool), the first pinch-off outside the box, or a mean area outside [40, 160] (NOT_MET)|inputs=K53, K54, K58, K59, K63|cost=77,568 sites, 128,000 steps, 6 to 9 min, plus 1 to 2 min preparation|from=L2-GP-09 kept; the drop observables were redefined on free components in the fix pass, because the draft rule (every cell at least 12 from every solid) put a drop under the tip, centre (40, 64), radius 8, entirely below y = 44, so the box [40, 56] and the y = 40 crossing were unreachable (final critic); the split and tie rules added in the second pass (verification)|json=0
PREDICT|id=HF-G10|kind=MODEL_EXACT|tag=DERIVED|control=NEGATIVE|fixed_by_inputs=0|statement=At equal levels (rung U0) the discrete G1 problem is exactly mirror-symmetric about the wall centre x = 104 (geometry, potential table, barrier, mirrors, initial guess and preparation; cell centres at (i + 1/2)/2 map to 208 - x). Integer addition is exact and commutative and each mirrored pair goes through the same operations, so the scheme keeps the symmetry bit for bit and releasing the barrier transfers nothing. The symmetric supercritical flowing case needs a mirror-doubled G1 and is not frozen.|predicted=at every record for t <= 2250: M_in(t) = M_out(t) as exact integers; sha256 of the state = sha256 of its mirror image; the same state hashes on 1, 2 and 4 threads|verdict_rule=MET if every record holds exactly|method=method.gp; run U0 of the ladder with a mirror hash at every record|falsifier=a single record with M_in != M_out, a mirror-hash mismatch or a thread-dependent hash (NOT_MET: an order-dependent or asymmetric code path)|inputs=K57, K58, K59|cost=shared with HF-G07 on 4 threads: 11 to 16 min; the reruns of U0 with its preparation on 1 and 2 threads add about 84 to 126 min (dispatch job); the push-time CI compares 1 against 4 threads only on the ci-threads subset (state hashes after 1024 or 4096 steps), so the full 1, 2 and 4 thread check of this row runs only in the dispatch job|from=L2-GP-11 kept; absorbs L3-08 (a) (judges); L3-09 dropped|json=0
PREDICT|id=HF-G11|kind=MECHANISM|tag=CONJECTURE|control=NEGATIVE|fixed_by_inputs=0|statement=Wetting ladder: attraction to the wall more strongly than to the liquid itself, made quantitative (Young-Dupre). sigma_wl(C3) from 1D strips at coexistence (mu0, g = 0, liquid far end); the dry wall is exactly empty (sigma_wv = 0) while V0 = C3/15.625 < 1/2. Young: cos theta = -sigma_wl/sigma_lv; S = -sigma_wl - sigma_lv; complete wetting iff S >= 0. The model has a wetting transition (lane 3's premise is false here); a weak wall partly wets, the T = 0 analog of He on Cs, with no wetting temperature as output. Sub-threshold walls are negative controls: they must not grow a film.|predicted=(a) engine 1D strips, on the wetting strip of K58 (z in [-4, 30], zero ghosts at the solid end, a liquid far end, started from phi = 1 at z > 0 and 0 at z <= 0 as gp1d.py, tau = 600), with sigma_wl = the sum over the free cells of [phi (-(1/2) L4 phi) + (U_w - mu0) rho + e(rho)] dz, the kinetic term consistent with the stencil: sigma_wl(C3 = 0, 1, 2, 3, 4, 6) = +0.2501, +0.1128, -0.0750, -0.2863, -0.5147, -1.0124, each +/- 0.01; S < 0 for C3 <= 2 and S > 0 for C3 >= 3 (S(2) = -0.1750, S(3) = +0.0363; threshold C3_w in (2, 3), interpolated 2.83); cos theta changes sign between C3 = 1 and 2. The finite strip is part of the definition: the longer strip z in [-4, 60] moves sigma_wl by -0.0014 at C3 = 3 and -0.0027 at C3 = 6, close to the -C3/(2 L^2) tail estimate. (b) G0 thin-seed runs: no film at h = 24 (coverage within 10 xi of the face <= 1e-3) for C3 = 1, 2 and 4; a film at h = 24 for C3 = 8 with s = 4.694 xi +/- 3 percent, also from the thick-slab start (1D design at h = 24 on z in [-4, 50] with the same energy: no film survives for C3 <= 3, a metastable film with Omega = +0.235 at C3 = 4, Omega = -0.148 at C3 = 6 and -0.599 at C3 = 8). (c) meniscus: the bath rho = 1/2 surface 3 xi from the face (the columns x = 61 and x = 83, each the mean of its two straddling columns, cell.edge), relative to y_L* = 32: in [-6, -0.5] for C3 = 1 (Young angle 116.8 degrees), in [+0.3, +5] for C3 = 2 (72.5 degrees), >= +3 for C3 = 4 (complete wetting at coexistence, film ending below h = 24)|verdict_rule=MET if (a) to (c) all hold|method=method.gp; the wetting strip of K58 at g = 0 and mu0, imaginary time from its liquid start (phi = 1 at z > 0, 0 at z <= 0) to tau = 600 (seconds each); the start is part of the definition: for C3 <= 6, V0 <= 0.384 < 1/2, so U_w - mu0 >= 1/2 - V0 > 0 everywhere and the dry strip is a stable state; from a seed start rho decays to it and sigma_wl reads 0, which misses every band of (a); at C3 = 0 the tau = 600 value is not converged (tau = 1200 lowers it by 1.05e-4), so there it also depends on the start and the integrator, by far less than the band; G0 imaginary time as HF-G02 at C3 = 1, 2, 4, 8 (thin seed) and 8 (thick slab)|falsifier=a film at h = 24 for C3 <= 4 or none at C3 = 8, an S sign pattern other than the frozen one, a sigma_wl outside its band, or a meniscus band missed (NOT_MET)|inputs=K53, K55, K57, K58 (analogy only: K34)|cost=1D strips seconds; 5 G0 runs of 2 to 4 min|from=replaces L3-03 (C3 ladder testing Young-Dupre; judge-lowT and referee); thresholds from the synthesis 1D design (wet4.txt); the fix pass froze the strip and the energy and recomputed (a) and the (b) design with the stencil-consistent kinetic term (exact_wet.py), which moves sigma_wl by +0.0012 at C3 = 0 up to +0.0118 at C3 = 6 against the draft np.diff values; the liquid start of the strip frozen in the second pass (verification)|json=0
PREDICT|id=HF-G12|kind=MECHANISM|tag=CONJECTURE|control=NEGATIVE|fixed_by_inputs=0|statement=Repulsive wall. In the wall-minus-liquid picture a wall weaker than helium gives a net repulsion, C3 < 0. Geometry G0d (G0 with the level at y = 64, mu = mu0 + 64 g), C3 = -32 on every solid. No film climbs, and below the level the liquid stands off the wall by a drying gap whose rho = 1/2 edge follows the mirrored law x_TF(D) = (abs(C3)/(g D))^(1/3) with the same kind of positive finite-width excess as the film.|predicted=(a) on every row with y >= 88 (24 above the level): max rho within 10 xi of either face <= 1e-6 (exact zero above about y = 94); (b) gap edge at depth D = 24, 32, 40 (y = 40, 32, 24): 7.1733, 6.5353, 6.0744 xi (1D reduced; x_TF = 6.9886, 6.3496, 5.8945), G0d within 2 percent of each (the depressed meniscus reaches about 11 below the level at the wall); (c) x(24)/x(40) within 1.5 percent of 1.18089|verdict_rule=MET if (a) to (c) all hold|method=method.gp; G0d imaginary time as HF-G02 from a liquid start below y = 64; the gap edge by integer linear interpolation of the first upward rho = 1/2 crossing; the rows y = 40, 32, 24 are cell edges, so each gap edge is the mean of the crossings on the two straddling rows (cell.edge), compared with the 1D values at the exact depth; the 1D values are row1d solutions with a liquid far end, started from phi = 1 at z > 0 (K58)|falsifier=a climbing film on a repulsive wall (the wall term is not applied as stated) or any band missed (NOT_MET)|inputs=K55, K57, K58|cost=one G0d run, 2 to 4 min|from=L3-02 restated for the self-bound model as a drying gap, no 2^(1/3) factor (judge-lowT); the (c) centre corrected from 1.18090 to 1.18089 in the fourth pass (verification)|json=0
PREDICT|id=HF-G13|kind=MECHANISM|tag=CONJECTURE|control=-|fixed_by_inputs=0|statement=C3 scaling on two faces of one wall. G0 with C3 = 64 on the left face (x = 64) and the cap half x < 72, C3 = 32 on the right face, the right cap half and the floor. At equal heights the thicker film follows C3^(1/3), slightly reduced by the finite-width excess, complementing HF-G02's height scaling.|predicted=s_64/s_32 at h = 24, 48, 96 = 1.2481, 1.2429, 1.2391 (1D reduced), each +/- 0.010; every ratio between 0.97 x 2^(1/3) = 1.2221 and 2^(1/3) = 1.2599|verdict_rule=MET if every ratio is in band|method=method.gp; G0 imaginary time as HF-G02, thin-seed start; the split is a per-face C3 on the single wall solid, not two touching solids: each cell takes C3 = 64 when its nearest point on the boundary of the union of solids (K55) lies on the left face or on the cap at x < 72, and C3 = 32 otherwise (ties to 32); the rows y = 56, 80, 128 are cell edges, so each thickness is the mean over the two straddling rows (cell.edge), compared with the 1D values at the exact h|falsifier=a ratio out of band (NOT_MET)|inputs=K55, K57, K58|cost=one G0 run, 2 to 4 min|from=L3-08 (b) restated on the rho = 1/2 crossing (judges; the referee 1D put the ratio 1.0 to 1.6 percent below 2^(1/3)); the per-face C3 rule frozen in the fix pass (final critic: two touching solids leave an attractive slot along the seam at x = 72)|json=0
PREDICT|id=HF-G14|kind=MECHANISM|tag=CONJECTURE|control=-|fixed_by_inputs=0|statement=Third sound on the GP film. Shelf geometry (solid floor y < 0, x in [0, 128] mirrored, g = 0, film at mu = mu0 - 3/16, the chemical potential 48 above a bath) with a standing thickness wave cos(pi x/128) (k s = 0.14). Its speed follows the model's film equation of state, c3^2 = Gamma dmu/dGamma = g Gamma/abs(dGamma/dh) (DERIVED for a 2D superfluid at long wavelength), and exceeds the incompressible sqrt(3 g h) because the dense superfluid wall layer is mobile; helium's inert solid layers (K39) act the other way.|predicted=c3_meas within 5 percent of c3_thermo from the engine's own 1D total coverages at h = 44 and 52 (design: Gamma_total(44, 48, 52) = 9.1316, 8.9215, 8.7298, c3_thermo = 0.833); c3_meas/sqrt(3 g 48) in [1.05, 1.17] (design 1.111; sqrt(3 g 48) = 0.75)|verdict_rule=MET if both hold|method=method.gp; imaginary-time preparation with mu(x) = mu0 - 3/16 + 0.003 cos(pi x/128); real time at uniform mu0 - 3/16 for 1240 (4 periods); c3 = omega/k from the first and last zero crossings of the mode coefficient of the coverage (integer cosine table)|falsifier=either band missed (NOT_MET)|inputs=K53, K55, K57, K58 (background only, no verdict: K39)|cost=14,336 sites, 79,360 steps, 1 to 2 min|from=new (judge-lowT: a missing row a film physicist expects)|json=0
PREDICT|id=HF-N01|kind=NUMERICS|tag=CONJECTURE|control=NEGATIVE|fixed_by_inputs=0|statement=The integrator's stability edge. RK4 is stable on the imaginary axis exactly for abs(lambda dt) <= 2 sqrt2 (K65). (a) Uniform periodic box (64 x 64 cells, dx = 1/2, psi = 1, mu_ref = mu0, V = 0: an exact stationary state at Q40) seeded with a (pi, pi) checkerboard of amplitude 2^-20 in Re psi; that mode's Bogoliubov frequency is exactly eps_max = sqrt(e0 (e0 + 2)) with e0 = 64/3 (K66), so dt* = 2 sqrt2/eps_max. (b) In situ: the U8 state at t = 64 with the same checkerboard seeded on every cell, fluid and solid, so the soft-core modes are seeded too (judge-lowT); spectral radius rho from power iteration on J^2 over the full grid (the Hamiltonian Jacobian has +/- i omega pairs, so power iteration on J itself does not converge; referee), rho = the square root of the dominant eigenvalue of -J^2, dt*_PI = 2 sqrt2/rho. Blow-up: the checkerboard component grows by 2^10 within 4000 steps; dt = k/2^16, bisection on k.|predicted=(a) eps_max = 22.310934, dt* = 0.12677314 (k* = 8308.2); dt_c/dt* in [0.995, 1.005]; at 0.97 dt* the mode decays (abs(R)^2 = 0.650 per step), at 1.03 dt* it grows (1.517 per step). (b) dt_c/dt*_PI in [0.97, 1.03]; the Rayleigh quotient changes by less than 1e-6 relative over the last 100 of >= 2000 iterations (printed); expected rho about 29.5 (soft core V = 8 plus the top kinetic eigenvalue 64/3), dt*_PI about 0.096|verdict_rule=MET if (a) and (b) hold|method=method.gp; power iteration on the real-linear Jacobian with the Rayleigh quotient at Q80; short runs from the frozen state at trial steps; an overflow-guard trip counts as blow-up|falsifier=a blow-up at or below 0.97 dt* (hidden stiffness: the nonlinear term or the wall stronger than stated) or none at 1.03 dt* (a weaker right-hand side, for example a missing factor in the Laplacian) (NOT_MET)|inputs=K57, K65, K66|cost=minutes: about 2000 RHS evaluations plus about 30 short runs of 4000 steps|from=L3-07 restated (exact uniform-box edge added; seeded core; J^2 iteration)|json=0
PREDICT|id=HF-N02|kind=NUMERICS|tag=CONJECTURE|control=-|fixed_by_inputs=0|statement=Positive engine control: Bogoliubov dispersion with the engine's own stencil. Uniform strip (256 x 2 cells, dx = 1/2, x in [0, 128] mirrored so cos(pi n x/128) are exact discrete modes; psi = 1, mu_ref = mu0, V = 0, C3 = 0, g = 0) seeded with Re psi = 1 + 2^-10 cos(k x). Lattice formula K66 (both judges: lane 3's 2nd-order symbol and 2 g n term fail this test by construction). Minimum eps/k over the lattice is c0, approached as k -> 0, so the GP Landau velocity is the sound speed.|predicted=eps at k = 0.0981748, 0.2945243, 0.9817477, 2.0125828 (n = 4, 12, 40, 82): 0.0982930, 0.2976999, 1.0932375, 2.8328401, each within 0.2 percent; eps/k >= 1 at all four and 1.001204 at the smallest; the 2nd-order symbol would miss k = 2.0126 by about 5.4 percent (planted fault)|verdict_rule=MET if every frequency lies within 0.2 percent of the lattice formula and eps/k >= 1 at every point|method=method.gp; the mode's density coefficient is evaluated at every step (dt = 1/64, K57) and each sign change is recorded (the two straddling steps and their raw coefficients), besides the 2-unit records: the n = 82 mode has a period of 2.2180, less than twice the 2-unit interval, so 2-unit records would read the alias pi - 2.8328 = 0.3088 rad per time unit and a correct engine would come out NOT_MET; per-step evaluation gives 141.95 samples per period of that mode, cannot alias a mode with eps below 64 sqrt6 = 156.7673 (one RK4 step turns its phase by less than pi) and reads any alias above 100.531 rad per time unit up to the stability edge (K57) and beyond it while y^2 < 6 + 2 sqrt3, where Re R(iy) < 0 still holds; a mode with a larger y grows by a factor of at least 1.776 per step (abs(R(iy))^2 rises with y^2 beyond 6), so the seeded mode trips the overflow guard within about 20 steps, any mode within about 60, and that run reads NOT_MET; so no fault can move a mode into a band by aliasing; frequency = pi (n_c - 1)/(t_last - t_first) over the n_c zero crossings of >= 200 periods, each crossing interpolated linearly between the two steps that straddle it; the formula evaluated with certified integer cosine bounds|falsifier=a frequency outside 0.2 percent (the kinetic or interaction term is not as stated) or eps/k < 1 (NOT_MET)|inputs=K52, K57, K66|cost=minutes (the smallest k needs about 820,000 steps on 512 sites)|from=L3-12 (a), (b) restated with the 4th-order symbol and lane 2's xi (both judges); per-step records in the fix pass (final critic); the alias reason corrected in the second pass (verification); the alias reach past the stability edge stated in the third pass (verification); the guard step count split into the seeded mode and any mode in the fourth pass (verification)|json=0
PREDICT|id=HF-L01|kind=HONEST_LIMIT|tag=CONJECTURE|control=-|fixed_by_inputs=0|statement=What the GP critical speed does and does not say about helium (MAPPED). With c0 = u1, n0 = rho(0 K) and m4: xi = 6.661e-11 m; helium's 315 A film is 472.9 xi, the GP film 4 to 7 xi. Two normalisations of the GP onset speed against helium's film v_c (0.17 to 0.39 m/s over HF-S07 and HF-S14): (1) Mach, v_lo/c0 against v_He/u1 <= 0.40/238.2; (2) K = v d m/hbar: helium 0.5 for Pickar-Atkins (0.330 to 0.772 for the measured rates), GP K_GP = v_lo s_top with s_top the measured cap-top thickness of U8: the mean over its records at t >= 64 of the outermost downward rho = 1/2 crossing above the cap on the cap-top column x = 104, measured from the exact solid surface, each the mean of the two straddling columns (cell.edge). The Mach mismatch of hundreds is mostly scale; in hbar/(m d) units the GP sits within a factor 2 to 12, which HF-L04 calls dimensional, not a validation. The real difference is the mechanism. The GP onset is intrinsic: a T = 0 barrier vanishes in a vortex-free film whose dense first layers are superfluid. Helium is a strongly correlated liquid whose first layers are solid (K39), and its onset is extrinsic, from remanent vortices, roughness and thermal activation; that last statement is uncited background and no verdict uses it. No helium v_c, film thickness at 1 cm or normal fraction comes from this lane; those need two-fluid hydrodynamics or path-integral Monte Carlo.|predicted=v_lo >= 0.1680 c0 (a Mach factor >= 100; expected 0.47 to 0.7 c0, a factor 280 to 420); K_GP in [1.0, 6.0]|verdict_rule=MET if both hold (v_lo = 0 if no rung is non-dissipative)|method=reader arithmetic in rationals on HF-G07's measured bracket (v_lo, the largest v_rim = q/Gamma_top over the records with 64 <= t <= t_end - 2 (where q is defined) of the non-dissipative rungs, HF-G07) and on s_top from the U8 records of HF-G05 at t >= 64, with K03, K06, K11, K14|falsifier=v_lo < 0.1680 c0 (for example vortices already in U16) or K_GP outside [1.0, 6.0] (NOT_MET)|inputs=K03, K06, K11, K12, K14, K23, K28, K31, K67 (background only, no verdict: K39)|cost=none beyond HF-G05 and HF-G07|from=L2-GP-10 merged with L3-11, retagged CONJECTURE, both normalisations (both judges); L3-11's TF-edge expectation dropped (cubic GP); v_lo read on records at t >= 64 in the third pass (verification); the records on which q is defined stated in the fourth pass (verification)|json=0
PREDICT|id=HF-L02|kind=HONEST_LIMIT|tag=DERIVED|control=-|fixed_by_inputs=1|statement=Rotons. Helium's Landau critical velocity is set by rotons, v_R = Delta/(hbar q0) (an upper bound on min E/p); it is not the film's critical velocity, and the GP has no roton, so its Landau velocity is the sound speed c0 (HF-N02). Claim 1: v_R/v_PA(315 A) >= 100: the film is limited by vortex nucleation far below the roton limit. Claim 2: in sound units the GP's Landau velocity exceeds helium's by at least 3.9 at both roton grid points, (v_L,GP/c0)/(v_R/u1) = u1/v_R >= 3.9. The threshold leaves a margin of 2.6558 percent at 1.1 K and 4.0322 percent at low T. That covers the rounding of the tabulated q0 to +/- 0.005 A^-1 (0.262 percent) and the spread of u1(0) values (238.21 against 238.30, 0.038 percent). The draft threshold 4.00 left 0.089 percent at 1.1 K, so a re-read of 0.1 percent could have flipped it.|predicted=v_R = 58.70959 m/s (8.61 K, 1.92 A^-1) and 59.49678 m/s (8.68 K, 1.91 A^-1); v_R/v_PA(315 A) = 233.1122 and 236.2379; u1/v_R = 4.05726 and 4.00358, both >= 3.9; each +/- 1 in the last digit|verdict_rule=MET if both claims hold on the certified intervals and the values lie in their bands|method=method.statics; exact k_B, hbar from h and the pi bracket; the margins (u1/v_R)/3.9 = [1.040322, 1.040323] at low T and [1.026558, 1.026559] at 1.1 K (exact_extra.py)|falsifier=a certified v_R/v_PA below 100 or a certified u1/v_R below 3.9 at either grid point (NOT_MET); a re-read of K14, K17 or K18 that puts u1/v_R below 3.9, which needs v_R/u1 to rise by a factor above (u1/v_R)/3.9, in [1.026558, 1.026559] at 1.1 K and [1.040322, 1.040323] at low T (by more than 2.6558 or 4.0322 percent), or puts v_R/v_PA below 100|inputs=K03, K05, K06, K08, K14, K17, K18, K31, K66|cost=under 1 s|from=lane1:HF-S11 (moved here, now on the verified Pickar-Atkins law) merged with L3-12 (c); claim 2 threshold 4.00 lowered to 3.9 at both grid points in the fix pass, with a matching falsifier (final critic)|json=0
PREDICT|id=HF-L03|kind=HONEST_LIMIT|tag=DERIVED|control=-|fixed_by_inputs=0|statement=Non-claims. The engine integrates the T = 0 GP for one classical field: 100 percent condensate and superfluid, no thermal component, entropy or temperature; it has self-binding and sigma = 1/4 by design. No receipt line may present as a GP output (i) helium's film v_c, (ii) rho_n/rho(T), (iii) T_lambda, (iv) the condensate fraction, (v) helium's drop size (HF-G09's 2D Tate law is model units only) or (vi) helium's film thickness at 1 cm. SI speeds or lengths appear only on MAPPED rows (HF-L01). Literature contrast only: rho_n/rho = 0.00700, 0.111, 0.553 at 1.0, 1.5, 2.0 K, T_lambda = 2.1768 K, sigma_lv = 3.544e-4 N/m. Even London's ideal Bose gas at helium's density misses T_lambda by 44 percent.|predicted=0 offending lines under the frozen audit rule; engine-defined rho_n/rho = 0 at every record; T_BEC = (2 pi hbar^2/(m4 k_B)) (n/zeta(3/2))^(2/3) at 0.1451397 g/cm^3 in [3.1363, 3.1364] K; T_BEC/T_lambda in [1.4408, 1.4409]|verdict_rule=MET if the audit finds no offending line and the certified intervals lie in their bands|method=frozen audit rule, fixed here before any engine code exists: the audit reads every line written by hf-gp or hf-read (receipts/GP-SHORT.hbp, receipts/long/*.hbp, receipts/READ.hbp); split each line into tokens, a token being a maximal run of characters other than the space, the bar, =, the full stop, comma, semicolon, colon, parentheses and square brackets; MAPPED rows are exempt (a MAPPED row is a line whose first field is MAPPED, and hf-read writes such rows only for HF-L01); every other line is offending if any of its tokens equals one of the SI unit tokens m/s, cm, nm, A, K, kg, J (case-sensitive), one of the words He or 4He (case-sensitive), or the words helium or Angstrom (any case); the audit checks only these tokens, so a compound such as cm^3/s or g/cm^3 is not one of them; hf-statics output and README.md are outside this rule, because they speak about helium by design (HF-L04 covers the README); method.statics; zeta(3/2) from a certified partial sum plus tail bound, the 2/3 power by integer root bracketing|falsifier=an offending line under the frozen audit rule, or a T_BEC interval outside the frozen one (NOT_MET)|inputs=K03, K05, K06, K08, K09, K11, K13, K15, K16, K33 (context, not used: K19)|cost=seconds|from=L3-10 restated: the claims of no self-binding and no surface tension and the drop-size non-claim (v) are corrected (both judges); the audit rule frozen in the fix pass (final critic); the full stop and Angstrom added to it in the second pass (verification)|json=0
PREDICT|id=HF-L04|kind=HONEST_LIMIT|tag=DERIVED|control=-|fixed_by_inputs=0|statement=Coincidence guard. At h = 1 cm and d = 315 A the film is near d* = 3 m4 C3_He/hbar^2, where two unrelated helium speeds nearly coincide: the Feynman vortex scale hbar/(m4 d) and the incompressible third-sound speed sqrt(3 g_n h). The measured film critical velocity and the measured transfer rates in units of hbar/m4 lie within a factor 5 of these scales. Any agreement within a factor 5 between a GP-derived speed in hbar/(m d) units and helium's v_c is therefore dimensional, not a validation, and no receipt may report it as one; this covers HF-S07 and HF-L01. Lane 3's third speed, the cubic-GP TF-edge speed (Anglin 2001), does not apply to this model and is dropped.|predicted=hbar/(m4 d) = 0.503702 m/s; sqrt(3 g_n h) = 0.542402 m/s; d* = 36.52621 nm, d/d* = 0.862395; sigma m4/hbar = 0.315127 (Seki zero head) and [0.674372, 0.737397] (Kwoh); each +/- 1 in the last digit; 0 offending lines under the frozen audit rule|verdict_rule=MET if the certified values lie in their bands and the audit finds no offending line|method=method.statics; square and cube roots by integer bracketing; frozen audit rule, fixed here before any engine code exists: the audit reads every line of receipts/STATICS.hbp, receipts/GP-SHORT.hbp, receipts/long/*.hbp, receipts/READ.hbp and README.md; after lowercasing, a line is offending if it contains the string 'validat' at any position where neither the six characters before it are 'not a ' nor the four characters before it are 'not ' (so 'is not a validation' and 'not validated' pass, while 'validates', 'validation of' and 'no validation' fail); the rule is broader than the claim on purpose: any un-negated validat counts, next to an agreement within a factor 5 or not|falsifier=a certified value outside its band, or an offending line under the frozen audit rule (NOT_MET)|inputs=K03, K04, K06, K08, K23, K28, HF-S02|cost=seconds|from=L3-14 restated on the pinned C3_He (315 A instead of a round 30 nm; both judges); the audit rule frozen in the fix pass (final critic)|json=0
